@page
@model PrivacyModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy Policy";
}
<h1>@ViewData["Title"]</h1>

<h2>Introduction</h2>
<p>
    PUBG Custom Stats ("we," "us," "our," or "Application") is committed to protecting your privacy. This Privacy Policy explains how our application collects, uses, and protects information you provide when using our service.
</p>

<h2>1. Information We Collect</h2>

<h3>1.1 Information from the PUBG API</h3>
<p>
    Our application retrieves player, match, and clan data from the PUBG API. This information is fetched based on your input and may include:
</p>
<ul>
    <li>Player names and PUBG account IDs</li>
    <li>Player statistics and match history</li>
    <li>Match data including timeline events, telemetry data, and game results</li>
    <li>Clan information and membership details</li>
    <li>Console/platform information (Xbox, PlayStation, PC, Mobile)</li>
    <li>Gamer tags associated with PUBG accounts</li>
</ul>

<h3>1.2 Information You Provide</h3>
<p>
    When using the application, you may provide:
</p>
<ul>
    <li>Your PUBG API key (required for accessing PUBG data)</li>
    <li>Player IDs and usernames for tracking</li>
    <li>Custom session names and match names</li>
    <li>Custom notes and descriptions for matches and sessions</li>
</ul>

<h2>2. How We Use Information</h2>
<p>
    The information collected is used exclusively for the following purposes:
</p>
<ul>
    <li>Retrieving and storing PUBG player and match statistics</li>
    <li>Generating custom statistics and analysis for your sessions and matches</li>
    <li>Creating kill matrices, charts, and performance summaries</li>
    <li>Organizing and tracking matches across multiple gaming sessions</li>
    <li>Displaying player clan affiliations and member statistics</li>
</ul>

<h2>3. Data Storage</h2>
<p>
    All data collected and retrieved is stored locally on your device or local server in a SQLite database. We do not transmit, store, or process this data on external servers, except:
</p>
<ul>
    <li>Communication with the PUBG API to retrieve publicly available player data</li>
    <li>Your PUBG API key is stored locally and used only to authenticate requests to PUBG's servers</li>
    <li>Publishing your custom statistics to the public leaderboard if you choose to do so</li>
</ul>

<h2>4. Data Retention</h2>
<p>
    Data is retained in your local database as long as you maintain the application. You may delete any data at any time by removing entries from the application or deleting the database.
</p>

<h2>5. Third-Party Services</h2>
<p>
    Our application relies on the PUBG API to retrieve public player and match data. Please refer to <a href="https://pubg.com/en/privacy" target="_blank">PUBG's Privacy Policy</a> for information on how PUBG handles your data.
</p>

<h2>6. Data Security</h2>
<p>
    Since data is stored locally on your device or network:
</p>
<ul>
    <li>You are responsible for securing access to your device and local network</li>
    <li>Your PUBG API key should be protected with the same care as a password</li>
    <li>Consider restricting database file access permissions appropriately</li>
</ul>

<h2>7. User Rights</h2>
<p>
    You have full control over your data:
</p>
<ul>
    <li><strong>Access:</strong> All data in the application is accessible to you through the UI</li>
    <li><strong>Modification:</strong> You can edit match names, session information, and custom notes</li>
    <li><strong>Deletion:</strong> You can delete any player, match, session, or season from the database</li>
    <li><strong>Export:</strong> You can export or back up your database as needed</li>
</ul>

<h2>8. What We Don't Do</h2>
<ul>
    <li>We do not sell, share, or monetize your data</li>
    <li>We do not use your data for advertising or marketing purposes</li>
    <li>We do not share your API key with third parties</li>
    <li>We do not track your activity outside of the application</li>
    <li>We do not collect personally identifiable information beyond what's provided by PUBG's API</li>
</ul>

<h2>9. Changes to This Policy</h2>
<p>
    We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. You will be notified of any significant changes through the application or in the release notes.
</p>

<h2>10. Contact</h2>
<p>
    If you have questions or concerns about this Privacy Policy or our privacy practices, please contact us through the application or via the project repository.
</p>

<h2>Acknowledgment</h2>
<p>
    By using PUBG Custom Stats, you acknowledge that you have read and understood this Privacy Policy and agree to its terms.
</p>

<p><em>Last Updated: August 2024</em></p>
